            <ArticleTitle>[Gastric necrosis following gastroplasty].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>718-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="INTRODUCTION" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Over the past ten years, laparoscopic surgery in the treatment of morbid obesity has expanded. However, there are few publications describing its side effects, notably the occurrence of gastric necrosis.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OBSERVATION" NlmCategory="METHODS">Two years after laparoscopic-banding for morbid obesity, a case of acute gastroenteritis in a 45 Year-old woman proved to be a gastric necrosis.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="COMMENTS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Relatively unknown, this complication is generally revealed by non-specific clinical signs. Only emergency oeso-gastro-duodenal opacification permits diagnosis. Early diagnosis permits conservative treatment before the onset of necrosis.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Care must be taken when using this technique, which has not yet proved its innocuousness, and regular follow-up of the patient is crucial.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
